.TH LSLOCALES 1 "August 2026" "lslocales 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lslocales \- list installed system locales
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lslocales
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lslocales
lists locales available on the host.
.PP
On Windows, identifiers are hex LCIDs from
.B EnumSystemLocales
and names come from
.B GetLocaleInfo
.RB ( LOCALE_SNAME ,
falling back to
.BR LOCALE_SLANGUAGE ).
On POSIX, names come from
.BR locale (1)
.RB ( \-a ),
with a directory-scan fallback.
.PP
Default output is one locale per line as
.IR id TAB name ,
sorted by name. When the id and name are identical a single column is
emitted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-names\-only
Emit locale names only.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-codes\-only
Emit locale identifiers only.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-supported
List supported locales rather than only installed locales (Windows). No-op
on POSIX when the inventory is not split.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-sort
Preserve enumeration order rather than sorting by name.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR locale (1)
.SH REPORTING BUGS
